See scratchpad/drag-cost-analysis.md for the verified mechanism and design rationale.

Summary:
 1. main.c ProcessNewFrame: skip the PrintWindow recapture trigger (WcMarkDirty) on
    move-only frames of an attached window; arm a settle recapture for when motion
    stops; allow a throttled refresh every PW_MOVE_RECAPTURE_MS mid-motion. The
    per-window buffer is position-invariant, so a pure move needs only MSG_CONFIGURE
    (already sent at input rate by the tracking path) — the daemon recomposites via
    XMoveResizeWindow + expose repaint from the stored image (xside.c:2072/1832/2477).
 2. main.c SynthUpdateMask: do not re-push a byte-identical mask — WcSetMask takes the
    engine lock exclusively (stalls behind an in-flight 15-18 ms PrintWindow) and
    forces a full recapture; a joint owner+child move computes an identical
    owner-relative mask at input rate.
 3. main.h / perwindow.c: new WINDOW_DATA fields + reset on channel attach/detach.

